# EC2 Setup – Cloud Ops Perspective

## Tasks Covered
- Launching EC2 instances
- Selecting instance types
- Key pair management
- Security group configuration
- Monitoring instance health

## Cloud Ops Notes
- EC2 instances should be monitored for CPU, memory, and disk usage
- Security groups act as virtual firewalls
- Stopped instances still incur EBS costs

## Troubleshooting Scenarios
- Instance unreachable due to incorrect security group
- High CPU usage due to workload spike
- Disk full issues on root volume
